<p><strong>A nail studio runs smoothly when clients book a named technician and a time online, each booking is checked against the schedule, and every payment is recorded as it happens.</strong></p>
<p><em>The scene below is a typical one, not a single named customer.</em></p>
<h2>The Saturday rush</h2>
<p>Gel, extensions, nail art and manicures all take different lengths of time. The phone rings, clients message on Instagram and walk-ins sit waiting. Two bookings land on the same technician, one client is left waiting for an hour, and the register does not show who paid for what.</p>
<h2>What goes wrong in a nail studio</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Different service lengths</strong> that the diary does not account for.</li><li><strong>Bookings from many places:</strong> phone, Instagram, WhatsApp and walk-ins.</li><li><strong>Unrecorded discounts and part-payments</strong> at the counter.</li></ul>
<h2>How it is solved</h2>
<p>Clients book the service, the technician and a free slot through <a href="/features/booking/">online booking</a>. Each booking checks the staff member and time, so there are no clashes. Payments, including part-payments, are recorded with the booking, and <a href="/features/discount-management/">discounts need approval</a>. Sell <a href="/features/packages/">packages</a> and <a href="/features/vouchers/">gift vouchers</a> and always know the balance.</p>
<h2>One studio or many</h2>
<p>Zennly works for a single studio and grows with you to several branches. See <a href="/solutions/salon/">software for salons and beauty parlours</a>.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Give every service a realistic duration.</li><li>Put one booking link in your Instagram bio.</li><li>Record every payment when it is taken.</li></ol>
